WEBVTT

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.768
Why potatoes?

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:06.601
Their first idea
was to clone Naomi,

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.972
but I suggested they start
with something smaller.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:22.250
Quite a feat of engineering.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.812
It's a Teirenian ant colony.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.653
I infused the soil
with a blue ion dye,

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.091
so it'd be easier
to see the insects.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.924
They're luminescent.

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.156
The drones produce

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.721
a fluorescent enzyme
that's activated

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:33.788
by the queen.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.232
Drones and queens?

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:38.270
I thought we were trying
to get these children away

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.430
from the Borg.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:40.973
The project was Mezoti's idea.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:43.474
I didn't want to discourage
her individuality.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.103
I like bugs.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.339
Well done.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:50.247
Let me know before
you take up beekeeping.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.414
What have we got here?

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.418
It's Kataris.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.476
Your father's planet.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.250
I've been learning all about it.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.314
Naomi programmed

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.485
the geophysical
and atmospheric conditions.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:04.189
There's quite a storm
in those mountains.

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:05.356
The Arpasian range

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:07.332
is known for high winds
and hail.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.425
I'll remember to bring my coat.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:17.101
Now, this looks impressive.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:18.940
It's a high-resolution

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.377
gravimetric sensor array.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:21.379
Ambitious.

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:22.540
It'll augment

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.446
our ability to scan
for the neutrino flux

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.711
associated with wormholes.

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:27.309
It could help Voyager

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.945
find a faster way home.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.489
The engineering principles
are sound.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:36.487
I expected these projects
to be interesting,

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.793
but this is truly exceptional.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.298
Thank you, Captain.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.960
I am very interested
in astrophysics.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:45.470
Well, you've obviously got
a knack for it.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.802
Well done.

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:51.207
How did you think of scanning
for neutrino fluctuations?

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.472
I've been studying
Starfleet records.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.343
He's a remarkable young man.

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:57.679
He hopes to earn
a permanent posting

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.274
in Astrometrics one day.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.479
I'm afraid that
won't be possible.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:04.022
Captain, the boy has
a unique talent.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.058
It's not a question of merit.

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:08.526
We've made contact
with his parents,

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:11.462
and I've set a course
for their planet.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.027
My scanner is calibrated
to pick up changes

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.899
in neutrino trajectories.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.962
That's good news.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:21.086
You've exceeded your scheduled
time here by one hour.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.286
I am almost finished.

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.386
Your work will have to wait.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:24.862
There's something
we need to discuss.

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:27.695
Look at this.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:37.200
It's a star forming
in the Orpisay nebula.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.268
The Orpisay nebula
is out of range

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.778
of our sensors.

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:43.338
I increased the resolution
of the long-range scanners.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:46.408
Impressive.

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:47.748
When I was on the cube,

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.881
I never thought
about what was outside...

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.220
pulsars,

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:54.385
quasars,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.724
nebulas...

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.127
but here in this lab,

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:01.963
I feel like I can see
the entire galaxy.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:06.867
What did you want
to talk to me about?

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.270
You said there was something

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:09.603
we needed to discuss.

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:11.803
Yes. That's correct.

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:18.280
It's time for you
to regenerate.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.930
Come in.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:41.802
I'd like the data
you've collected

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.136
on Icheb's species

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:45.473
so I can prepare him
for reassimilation.

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:47.478
Maybe we could refer to it

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:50.675
as "getting reacquainted
with his family."

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.479
If you prefer.

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:55.487
I'll transfer the files
to Astrometrics.

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:56.954
Thank you.

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:59.115
How'd he take the news?

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:04.128
You haven't told him.

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:06.859
No.

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.457
Why not?

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:11.196
It won't be easy for him
to accept.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.830
He's adapted to life on Voyager.

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:16.500
And you've adapted
to having him here.

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:18.544
My feelings are irrelevant.

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:19.942
Are they?

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:26.614
Would you like me to tell him?

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:29.621
It's my responsibility...

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:32.852
but I am uncertain
how to proceed.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.689
Well, you've already
helped him make

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:37.730
one difficult transition.

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:39.355
How did you do that?

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:42.663
By giving him the benefit
of my own experiences,

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:46.535
encouraging him to be resilient
in the face of obstacles.

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:51.410
Sounds like a good strategy.

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.838
Is your alcove
malfunctioning?

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:27.846
I'm calculating
neutrino trajectories.

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:29.814
You need to regenerate.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.644
Very well.

00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:37.582
Wait.

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:42.654
We've located your parents.

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:45.196
Voyager is due to
arrive at their planet

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:46.561
tomorrow.

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:51.530
Do I have to stay with them?

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:54.539
They're your parents.

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:56.768
I don't remember them.

00:07:58.678 --> 00:08:00.305
After my parents
were assimilated,

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:03.041
I never saw them again.

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:05.242
You're fortunate
to have this chance.

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:07.218
What about the others?

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:08.480
We haven't been able

00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:10.283
to locate their families yet.

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:11.789
That's not what I mean.

00:08:11.858 --> 00:08:14.793
What will happen to them
if I leave?

00:08:14.861 --> 00:08:16.351
They depend on me.

00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:18.056
They'll adapt.

00:08:23.603 --> 00:08:26.071
I'll never see you again?

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:30.806
I've been studying
Brunali culture.

00:08:30.877 --> 00:08:32.208
It's very different

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:35.076
from what you've become
accustomed to on Voyager.

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:36.444
In what way?

00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:39.314
They're an
agrarian society.

00:08:39.385 --> 00:08:42.718
Their technological
resources are limited.

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:45.416
Are they capable
of space travel?

00:08:45.491 --> 00:08:47.618
Yes, but most of their vessels

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:49.627
were destroyed by the Borg.

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:52.027
How will I continue my studies?

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:55.801
I don't know.

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:03.666
Icheb...

00:09:22.428 --> 00:09:24.521
I'm detecting
scattered enclaves

00:09:24.597 --> 00:09:26.360
on the northern continent...

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:27.694
all with populations

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:29.132
of fewer than 10,000.

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:31.066
Judging from the residual
gamma radiation,

00:09:31.137 --> 00:09:32.399
it appears they've suffered

00:09:32.471 --> 00:09:35.406
numerous Borg attacks
over the past decade.

00:09:35.474 --> 00:09:36.907
That's not surprising.

00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:39.534
There's a Borg transwarp conduit
less than a light-year away.

00:09:39.612 --> 00:09:42.137
Not exactly prime real estate.

00:09:42.214 --> 00:09:44.876
Tuvok, run continuous scans
for Borg activity.

00:09:44.951 --> 00:09:46.714
Tom, put us into
synchronous orbit.

00:09:46.786 --> 00:09:49.380
Yes, ma'am.

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:51.013
Seven, you'd better get Icheb.

00:09:59.665 --> 00:10:02.793
According to these scans,
you're in perfect health.

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:05.462
Then why does my stomach
feel so strange?

00:10:05.538 --> 00:10:08.006
Hmm.

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.103
Oh, I should have known.

00:10:13.179 --> 00:10:15.739
You've got butterflies
in there.

00:10:15.815 --> 00:10:18.409
I never assimilated
butterflies.

00:10:18.484 --> 00:10:20.577
It's an expression used

00:10:20.653 --> 00:10:23.349
to describe anxiety
or apprehension,

00:10:23.422 --> 00:10:26.118
both of which are
perfectly natural reactions

00:10:26.192 --> 00:10:29.093
for someone about to meet
his long-lost parents.

00:10:29.161 --> 00:10:30.423
If it's any comfort,

00:10:30.496 --> 00:10:33.465
I'm sure they're just
as nervous about meeting you.

00:10:33.532 --> 00:10:34.829
Parents are irrelevant.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.299
Really.

00:10:36.369 --> 00:10:38.769
Do you think Naomi's mother
is irrelevant to her?

00:10:38.838 --> 00:10:41.966
I have Seven of Nine to
assist me in my education.

00:10:42.074 --> 00:10:44.406
I have you to care
for my medical needs.

00:10:45.511 --> 00:10:49.641
Your parents can nurture you
in ways this crew can't.

00:10:49.715 --> 00:10:51.615
They can explain
the Brunali culture,

00:10:51.684 --> 00:10:53.311
share their experiences
with you.

00:10:53.386 --> 00:10:54.683
You didn't have parents.

00:10:54.754 --> 00:10:55.846
No, but...

00:10:55.921 --> 00:10:57.946
You adapted to serve
a vital function

00:10:58.024 --> 00:10:59.457
aboard this vessel,

00:10:59.525 --> 00:11:01.516
forged relationships
with its crew...

00:11:01.594 --> 00:11:03.585
all without the
benefit of parents.

00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:05.756
I had my programming
to fall back on.

00:11:05.831 --> 00:11:08.425
And how would your
programming respond

00:11:08.501 --> 00:11:11.231
if you were asked to
live with strangers?

00:11:14.874 --> 00:11:16.933
Are you damaged?

00:11:17.076 --> 00:11:18.668
He's fine.

00:11:18.744 --> 00:11:21.144
I was just giving him
a last-minute checkup.

00:11:22.615 --> 00:11:23.946
It's time.

00:11:26.919 --> 00:11:29.581
The "butterflies" will go away.

00:12:07.026 --> 00:12:08.288
Hello.

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:09.918
I'm Captain Janeway.

00:12:10.029 --> 00:12:11.792
Icheb.

00:12:11.864 --> 00:12:14.230
You've... grown.

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:16.359
He spent several months
in a Borg

00:12:16.435 --> 00:12:18.130
maturation chamber.

00:12:19.705 --> 00:12:21.570
This is Seven of Nine.

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:24.404
That's a Borg designation,
isn't it?

00:12:24.477 --> 00:12:27.503
Like your son, I was liberated
from the collective.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.639
Seven has been instrumental
in helping Icheb

00:12:29.715 --> 00:12:30.943
make his transition.

00:12:31.016 --> 00:12:32.381
Then we're very grateful

00:12:32.451 --> 00:12:33.543
to you.

00:12:33.619 --> 00:12:35.746
I'm Leucon, Icheb's father.

00:12:35.821 --> 00:12:38.312
This is his mother, Yifay.

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.358
How are you?

00:12:40.426 --> 00:12:42.860
Fine.

00:12:44.396 --> 00:12:45.886
Do these hurt you?

00:12:47.399 --> 00:12:48.764
No.

00:12:52.938 --> 00:12:56.669
We're very happy to
have you back with us.

00:12:56.742 --> 00:12:58.767
Mala, Remi,

00:12:58.844 --> 00:12:59.970
Yivel.

00:13:00.112 --> 00:13:02.376
Welcome home, Icheb.

00:13:09.021 --> 00:13:10.147
I would like

00:13:10.222 --> 00:13:11.883
to return to Voyager now.

00:13:26.372 --> 00:13:28.806
Thank you for coming.

00:13:28.874 --> 00:13:30.307
Where's Icheb?

00:13:30.376 --> 00:13:31.934
I thought
it might be better

00:13:32.044 --> 00:13:33.705
if we talked
ourselves first.

00:13:33.779 --> 00:13:36.714
What exactly is
there to discuss?

00:13:36.782 --> 00:13:40.741
How to make this transition
easier for your son.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:42.879
Please, sit down.

00:13:47.426 --> 00:13:49.860
It won't be easy for him

00:13:49.929 --> 00:13:51.897
to give up the luxuries
of your ship.

00:13:51.964 --> 00:13:54.364
It's more than a
question of luxuries.

00:13:54.433 --> 00:13:57.061
Icheb has special medical needs.

00:13:57.136 --> 00:13:59.297
We have a physician
in our settlement.

00:13:59.371 --> 00:14:02.101
We should arrange for him
to consult with our Doctor.

00:14:02.174 --> 00:14:03.471
He also requires

00:14:03.542 --> 00:14:04.702
daily regeneration.

00:14:04.777 --> 00:14:07.245
I'm sure you can adapt
some of our technology

00:14:07.313 --> 00:14:08.575
to make that possible.

00:14:08.647 --> 00:14:10.706
What about his
educational needs?

00:14:10.783 --> 00:14:12.375
Our children go to school.

00:14:12.451 --> 00:14:13.918
Well he be able to continue
his studies

00:14:13.986 --> 00:14:15.453
in astrometrics
and spatial harmonics?

00:14:15.521 --> 00:14:17.386
If Icheb has an
aptitude for science,

00:14:17.456 --> 00:14:18.388
I'm sure he'll find

00:14:18.457 --> 00:14:20.448
that we have a great
deal to teach him.

00:14:20.526 --> 00:14:22.585
For example?

00:14:22.661 --> 00:14:23.923
We've developed
sophisticated

00:14:24.029 --> 00:14:26.054
techniques
in agricultural genetics,

00:14:26.131 --> 00:14:29.794
which allow us to grow crops
in an inhospitable environment.

00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:31.302
Icheb has expressed no interest

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:32.632
in agriculture.

00:14:32.705 --> 00:14:35.173
I'm sure, once he's been exposed
to the subject,

00:14:35.241 --> 00:14:36.936
he'll find it quite challenging.

00:14:37.076 --> 00:14:39.567
There's still the issue
of his safety.

00:14:39.645 --> 00:14:42.136
We're perfectly capable
of protecting our son.

00:14:42.214 --> 00:14:44.648
Your proximity to a Borg conduit

00:14:44.717 --> 00:14:46.810
makes you extremely vulnerable.

00:14:46.886 --> 00:14:49.116
I'm curious if you've
ever considered relocating.

00:14:49.188 --> 00:14:49.847
Seven.

00:14:49.922 --> 00:14:50.854
No.

00:14:50.923 --> 00:14:52.356
It's all right, Captain.

00:14:52.424 --> 00:14:53.948
This planet is our home.

00:14:54.059 --> 00:14:55.526
We will never leave it.

00:14:55.594 --> 00:14:57.528
We will defend it
against the Borg,

00:14:57.596 --> 00:15:00.429
or anyone else who threatens us.

00:15:00.499 --> 00:15:02.433
Your courage is admirable
but unrealistic.

00:15:02.501 --> 00:15:04.093
Wait for me in my ready room.

00:15:04.169 --> 00:15:06.103
Captain...
Now.

00:15:19.652 --> 00:15:21.711
I apologize for her behavior.

00:15:21.787 --> 00:15:23.687
She and Icheb have
grown very close,

00:15:23.756 --> 00:15:25.485
but that's no excuse
for rudeness.

00:15:25.557 --> 00:15:27.491
We'd like to see
our son now.

00:15:28.894 --> 00:15:30.623
Please be patient.

00:15:30.696 --> 00:15:33.756
If we rush things,
your next encounter with him

00:15:33.832 --> 00:15:36.198
may not go any better
than the last.

00:15:36.268 --> 00:15:38.168
Stay aboard Voyager for a while.

00:15:38.237 --> 00:15:41.365
It'll give Icheb a
chance to get to know you

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.908
in an environment
that's familiar to him.

00:15:43.976 --> 00:15:46.206
I'll have Neelix
do everything he can

00:15:46.278 --> 00:15:48.872
to make you comfortable
while you're here.

00:15:55.387 --> 00:15:58.550
Your attitude is making
a difficult situation worse.

00:15:58.624 --> 00:16:00.524
I was simply
attempting to ensure

00:16:00.592 --> 00:16:01.854
Icheb's well-being.

00:16:01.927 --> 00:16:03.087
By insulting his parents?

00:16:03.162 --> 00:16:04.857
Those issues needed
to be discussed.

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:07.057
You could've done it
with a little more tact.

00:16:07.132 --> 00:16:09.259
Perhaps. But that
doesn't alter the fact

00:16:09.335 --> 00:16:12.327
that those individuals may
not be suitable guardians.

00:16:12.404 --> 00:16:14.895
Those individuals are
his mother and father.

00:16:14.974 --> 00:16:15.906
Which is no guarantee

00:16:15.975 --> 00:16:17.567
that they'll be able
to care for him.

00:16:17.643 --> 00:16:19.338
He's far more
likely to flourish

00:16:19.411 --> 00:16:20.742
if he remains on Voyager.

00:16:20.813 --> 00:16:22.747
That's not an option, Seven.

00:16:23.782 --> 00:16:25.181
Are you ordering
him off the ship...

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:26.182
That's not what I said...

00:16:26.251 --> 00:16:27.513
...so that he can be
assimilated again?

00:16:27.586 --> 00:16:29.417
What makes you so sure
that's going to happen?

00:16:29.488 --> 00:16:31.718
They shouldn't remain
on that planet.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:32.620
It's their home.

00:16:32.691 --> 00:16:34.124
It's not worth protecting.

00:16:34.193 --> 00:16:36.855
Who are you to decide that?

00:16:38.197 --> 00:16:40.290
Anyone who values
their own goals

00:16:40.366 --> 00:16:43.733
over the safety of their
children is irresponsible.

00:16:43.802 --> 00:16:47.465
Are we talking
about Icheb's parents or yours?

00:16:47.539 --> 00:16:49.632
Both.

00:16:56.248 --> 00:16:59.149
It's not like you to admit
to something like that.

00:16:59.218 --> 00:17:03.086
It would be naive for me to
claim objectivity in this case,

00:17:03.155 --> 00:17:06.090
but I'm not prepared
to return Icheb to parents

00:17:06.158 --> 00:17:08.183
who may be as careless
as my own.

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:10.251
I know what it's like
to feel protective

00:17:10.329 --> 00:17:13.321
towards someone you've helped
through a difficult period.

00:17:15.267 --> 00:17:18.293
But Icheb is an individual now.

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.338
You have to give him a chance

00:17:20.406 --> 00:17:22.704
to form
his own opinions.

00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:26.105
If I do...

00:17:26.178 --> 00:17:29.272
and he decides to
remain on Voyager...

00:17:29.348 --> 00:17:32.613
Then it'll be my problem.

00:17:34.887 --> 00:17:37.355
Is your mother pretty?

00:17:37.423 --> 00:17:39.550
What are they like?

00:17:39.625 --> 00:17:41.217
I'm busy.

00:17:41.293 --> 00:17:43.386
I never met my father.

00:17:43.462 --> 00:17:45.555
I don't remember ours.

00:17:45.631 --> 00:17:47.599
Neither do I.

00:17:47.666 --> 00:17:49.531
Are you going to stay with them?

00:17:49.601 --> 00:17:51.831
If you leave,

00:17:51.904 --> 00:17:54.532
who is going to help us
with our science projects?

00:17:54.606 --> 00:17:56.301
If you don't stop
asking questions,

00:17:56.375 --> 00:17:58.843
I'm going to put all of you
in a cargo container

00:17:58.911 --> 00:18:00.037
and transport you back

00:18:00.112 --> 00:18:01.739
to the Borg.

00:18:08.487 --> 00:18:10.387
Come with me.

00:18:10.456 --> 00:18:12.014
Where?

00:18:12.091 --> 00:18:13.888
To dinner with your parents.

00:18:13.959 --> 00:18:15.051
I'm working.

00:18:15.127 --> 00:18:17.186
You can continue
your work after the meal.

00:18:17.262 --> 00:18:20.823
I don't have anything
to talk about with them.

00:18:20.899 --> 00:18:23.493
Then it will be
a very quiet evening.

00:18:23.569 --> 00:18:25.799
I'm not going.

00:18:25.871 --> 00:18:28.032
Your attendance is not optional.

00:18:59.638 --> 00:19:01.265
Enjoy your meal.

00:19:05.644 --> 00:19:07.578
Come, sit down.

00:19:09.281 --> 00:19:10.873
I prefer to stand.

00:19:12.684 --> 00:19:16.586
Mr. Neelix let me use his galley
to prepare some poma.

00:19:16.655 --> 00:19:18.589
I'm not hungry.

00:19:20.259 --> 00:19:23.490
It was your favorite food
when you were little.

00:19:23.562 --> 00:19:25.553
I'm not little anymore.

00:19:26.999 --> 00:19:28.864
No.

00:19:28.934 --> 00:19:31.801
No, you're not.

00:19:34.239 --> 00:19:39.643
Your mother worked hard
on that meal.

00:19:39.711 --> 00:19:41.804
Couldn't you at least try it?

00:20:20.052 --> 00:20:21.349
Good.

00:20:23.188 --> 00:20:24.621
Isn't it?

00:20:31.196 --> 00:20:33.460
Nice to see the family
back together again,

00:20:33.532 --> 00:20:34.829
isn't it?

00:20:36.535 --> 00:20:38.765
When you were little,
you would only eat...

00:20:56.822 --> 00:20:58.949
The Borg didn't leave us
much to work with,

00:20:59.024 --> 00:21:02.482
but we didn't need much,
just a little ingenuity.

00:21:02.561 --> 00:21:05.428
Everything you see,
we built with our own hands...

00:21:05.497 --> 00:21:08.591
our homes, cultivation bays...

00:21:08.667 --> 00:21:10.601
What's this?

00:21:10.669 --> 00:21:12.830
A genetic resequencer.

00:21:12.904 --> 00:21:15.395
We use it to alter the
DNA of certain plants

00:21:15.474 --> 00:21:17.738
to conform with
environmental conditions.

00:21:17.809 --> 00:21:19.333
You built this as well.

00:21:19.411 --> 00:21:21.675
We adapted parts
from damaged vessels.

00:21:21.747 --> 00:21:23.806
Nothing's been wasted.

00:21:23.882 --> 00:21:25.440
Efficient.

00:21:25.517 --> 00:21:28.918
Efficiency's one attribute
we share with the Borg.

00:21:28.987 --> 00:21:31.012
In our case,
it's a necessity.

00:21:33.525 --> 00:21:36.756
I know our settlement
seems primitive...

00:21:36.828 --> 00:21:38.762
compared to Voyager,

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:41.390
but I promise you,
that will change.

00:21:41.466 --> 00:21:42.797
What about space travel?

00:21:42.868 --> 00:21:44.802
Someday...

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:46.633
we'll have ships
that rival Voyager,

00:21:46.705 --> 00:21:48.070
but we need the dedication

00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:49.971
of young people like you
to help us.

00:21:50.075 --> 00:21:51.975
Icheb!

00:21:52.077 --> 00:21:53.476
How are you?

00:21:53.545 --> 00:21:55.945
Well! Thank you!

00:21:56.014 --> 00:21:58.778
Maybe later you can join us
up on the field

00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:00.784
for a game of pala!

00:22:02.788 --> 00:22:05.052
I don't remember how to play!

00:22:05.123 --> 00:22:07.523
It will come back to you!

00:22:09.461 --> 00:22:11.725
You used to be
quite an athlete.

00:22:14.099 --> 00:22:15.930
You can make
a difference here, Icheb.

00:22:16.034 --> 00:22:18.161
I don't know anything
about agriculture...

00:22:18.236 --> 00:22:19.828
or genetics.

00:22:19.905 --> 00:22:22.169
It won't take you long to learn,

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:24.037
not with a mind like yours.

00:22:25.811 --> 00:22:27.938
It's time to return to Voyager.

00:22:28.046 --> 00:22:30.378
I am staying here tonight.

00:22:30.449 --> 00:22:32.815
They don't have
a regeneration unit.

00:22:32.884 --> 00:22:34.852
We're going to have
to install one eventually.

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:36.478
Might as well do it now.

00:22:37.889 --> 00:22:39.220
As far as I'm aware,

00:22:39.291 --> 00:22:41.054
he hasn't decided
to remain here yet.

00:22:41.126 --> 00:22:43.560
But he has asked
to stay tonight.

00:22:46.832 --> 00:22:48.697
Return with me to the ship.

00:22:48.767 --> 00:22:50.496
We'll prepare
a regeneration unit.

00:22:56.141 --> 00:22:57.870
I've adapted
this neural transceiver

00:22:57.943 --> 00:23:00.104
to interface
with the portable regenerator.

00:23:00.178 --> 00:23:03.545
It has enough power
to complete one full cycle.

00:23:03.615 --> 00:23:06.311
We'll have to devise
a way of recharging it.

00:23:06.385 --> 00:23:08.683
If Icheb decides to stay.

00:23:12.224 --> 00:23:14.522
My wife and I appreciate

00:23:14.593 --> 00:23:16.458
everything you've
done for our son.

00:23:16.528 --> 00:23:18.257
It's obvious you
care about him.

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:20.855
He's a unique individual.

00:23:20.932 --> 00:23:22.900
Yes, he is.

00:23:22.968 --> 00:23:25.266
To get him back is... well...

00:23:25.337 --> 00:23:27.134
a miracle.

00:23:28.507 --> 00:23:31.067
How was he taken?

00:23:35.213 --> 00:23:37.147
Since the Borg
first attacked us,

00:23:37.215 --> 00:23:40.707
we've taken great pains
to hide whatever new technology

00:23:40.786 --> 00:23:41.946
we develop.

00:23:42.053 --> 00:23:44.419
So that passing cubes won't be
attracted to your planet.

00:23:44.489 --> 00:23:48.255
Unfortunately, we haven't
always been successful.

00:23:50.629 --> 00:23:54.326
One morning, about
four years ago...

00:23:57.269 --> 00:23:58.827
Icheb heard me talking

00:23:58.904 --> 00:24:01.099
about a new
fertilization array

00:24:01.173 --> 00:24:03.767
we'd constructed
in the lower field.

00:24:03.842 --> 00:24:06.037
He wanted to see it.

00:24:06.111 --> 00:24:07.738
I told him I'd take
him the next day.

00:24:09.448 --> 00:24:11.616
But he was impatient,
the way boys can be.

00:24:11.683 --> 00:24:14.709
I never even realized
he'd wandered off

00:24:14.786 --> 00:24:16.651
when the alarm sounded.

00:24:16.721 --> 00:24:20.248
It turns out the Borg
were just as interested

00:24:20.325 --> 00:24:23.123
in our new technology
as Icheb was.

00:24:24.629 --> 00:24:26.563
They took him...

00:24:26.631 --> 00:24:28.030
assimilated everyone

00:24:28.099 --> 00:24:30.499
in the area.

00:24:30.569 --> 00:24:34.096
Oh. If only I'd kept
a closer eye on him.

00:24:34.172 --> 00:24:37.471
Icheb has a mind of his own.

00:24:39.010 --> 00:24:40.568
But still...

00:24:40.645 --> 00:24:43.478
it's hard not to blame myself.

00:24:43.548 --> 00:24:46.676
Your parents must've felt
the same way when they lost you.

00:24:46.751 --> 00:24:50.778
My parents were with me
when the Borg attacked.

00:24:50.856 --> 00:24:53.586
I can't imagine what that
must've been like for them,

00:24:53.658 --> 00:24:55.922
watching their daughter
being assimilated...

00:24:55.994 --> 00:24:58.792
helpless to defend her?

00:24:58.864 --> 00:25:02.664
It's important that Icheb
regenerate for six uninterrupted

00:25:02.734 --> 00:25:04.895
hours.

00:25:05.003 --> 00:25:06.630
I understand.

00:25:06.705 --> 00:25:07.899
He may resist.

00:25:08.006 --> 00:25:10.566
He doesn't like to waste time.

00:25:12.043 --> 00:25:15.376
I have had to contend with
his lack of patience as well.

00:25:17.682 --> 00:25:21.675
Over there is a star
called Kelsin III,

00:25:21.753 --> 00:25:24.916
and to the west is
the Orlitus Cluster.

00:25:25.023 --> 00:25:27.321
There, just above it,

00:25:27.392 --> 00:25:29.826
when you connect
those six stars,

00:25:29.895 --> 00:25:32.796
they form what we call
the Great Horn.

00:25:36.001 --> 00:25:37.969
I see it.

00:25:39.337 --> 00:25:41.134
You inherited your love

00:25:41.206 --> 00:25:43.674
of the stars from your father.

00:25:43.742 --> 00:25:45.937
Being on that starship,

00:25:46.077 --> 00:25:49.672
you learned much more
about astronomy than I have.

00:25:49.748 --> 00:25:51.477
Our little window can't compare

00:25:51.550 --> 00:25:53.313
to Voyager's Astrometrics Lab.

00:25:53.385 --> 00:25:54.579
No.

00:25:54.653 --> 00:25:56.416
But it's nice.

00:25:58.056 --> 00:25:59.648
You see?

00:25:59.724 --> 00:26:03.182
We have everything
we need right here...

00:26:03.261 --> 00:26:08.699
a warm fire, good food
that we grow ourselves,

00:26:08.767 --> 00:26:11.167
and people who love us.

00:26:11.236 --> 00:26:13.727
Icheb has people on Voyager

00:26:13.805 --> 00:26:15.636
who love him, too.

00:26:18.276 --> 00:26:20.801
You've grown attached
to the crew on that ship,

00:26:20.879 --> 00:26:22.244
haven't you?

00:26:22.314 --> 00:26:26.080
They've provided for me,
given me opportunities.

00:26:26.151 --> 00:26:28.278
They're good people...

00:26:28.353 --> 00:26:31.345
people who've experienced
hardship themselves.

00:26:31.423 --> 00:26:33.357
Seven of Nine

00:26:33.425 --> 00:26:36.087
told me
about your science project.

00:26:36.161 --> 00:26:38.925
She said it might prove
very useful.

00:26:38.997 --> 00:26:41.431
It's designed
to detect wormholes.

00:26:41.499 --> 00:26:43.933
How will that benefit them?

00:26:44.002 --> 00:26:46.664
It may help them find
a way back to Earth.

00:26:46.738 --> 00:26:48.797
Why is that so important
to them?

00:26:51.843 --> 00:26:53.777
It's their home.

00:26:58.283 --> 00:26:59.716
Interesting, isn't it?

00:26:59.784 --> 00:27:01.877
What?

00:27:01.987 --> 00:27:04.353
With all their technology,

00:27:04.422 --> 00:27:08.688
their opportunity
to explore the galaxy,

00:27:08.760 --> 00:27:12.355
the thing they want most
is to get home.

00:27:21.973 --> 00:27:23.702
Good morning.

00:27:23.775 --> 00:27:26.175
Did you regenerate
successfully?

00:27:26.244 --> 00:27:28.439
Yes, and I slept...

00:27:28.513 --> 00:27:31.038
under the stars.

00:27:31.116 --> 00:27:33.050
You should try it.

00:27:33.118 --> 00:27:35.814
You weren't in
class this morning.

00:27:35.887 --> 00:27:37.616
The others missed you.

00:27:39.824 --> 00:27:41.815
I was helping my father.

00:27:43.662 --> 00:27:46.130
There is something
we need to discuss.

00:27:50.368 --> 00:27:52.336
What is it?

00:27:55.774 --> 00:27:57.901
You've decided
to stay with them.

00:27:59.978 --> 00:28:01.309
Yes.

00:28:01.379 --> 00:28:03.745
You're certain?

00:28:03.815 --> 00:28:06.010
This is my home.

00:28:06.084 --> 00:28:09.212
I have a responsibility
to help them rebuild it.

00:28:11.589 --> 00:28:13.523
I'll inform the Captain.

00:28:13.591 --> 00:28:15.559
Thank you.

00:28:17.328 --> 00:28:19.353
I'm sure you'll want
to say good-bye

00:28:19.431 --> 00:28:21.399
to the other children.

00:28:36.614 --> 00:28:37.876
Inside, you'll find padds

00:28:37.949 --> 00:28:40.213
containing data on
a variety of subjects

00:28:40.285 --> 00:28:43.413
that will allow you to
continue your studies.

00:28:43.488 --> 00:28:47.424
I've also included a
high-resolution telescope.

00:28:47.492 --> 00:28:49.790
It's a poor substitute
for astrometric sensors.

00:28:49.861 --> 00:28:51.522
I will use it every day.

00:29:01.306 --> 00:29:04.070
Good-bye, Icheb, and good luck.

00:29:04.142 --> 00:29:06.633
Thank you, Captain.

00:29:06.711 --> 00:29:08.906
I hope you find a way home.

00:30:05.470 --> 00:30:06.732
Warning.

00:30:06.805 --> 00:30:09.103
Regeneration cycle incomplete.

00:30:13.578 --> 00:30:14.943
What is it?

00:30:15.079 --> 00:30:17.445
I can't regenerate.

00:30:18.516 --> 00:30:19.505
Warning.

00:30:19.584 --> 00:30:21.074
Explain.

00:30:21.152 --> 00:30:22.847
Regeneration cycle incomplete.

00:30:22.921 --> 00:30:24.912
I miss Icheb.

00:30:26.558 --> 00:30:28.549
So do I...

00:30:28.626 --> 00:30:30.218
but we'll adapt.

00:30:30.295 --> 00:30:31.956
Now return to your alcove.

00:30:32.030 --> 00:30:36.091
If you find my parents,
will I have to go with them?

00:30:36.167 --> 00:30:40.103
We'll discuss that
when and if the time comes.

00:30:40.171 --> 00:30:43.299
I hope you don't find them.

00:30:45.743 --> 00:30:47.404
Regenerate.

00:30:53.852 --> 00:30:55.786
Seven?

00:30:55.854 --> 00:30:57.412
Yes?

00:30:57.488 --> 00:31:00.150
What if the Borg try to
assimilate Icheb again?

00:31:00.225 --> 00:31:01.886
His people lack resources.

00:31:01.960 --> 00:31:05.418
The Borg have little reason
to return to their planet.

00:31:05.496 --> 00:31:08.124
What if Icheb's on a ship?

00:31:08.199 --> 00:31:09.826
Unlikely.

00:31:09.901 --> 00:31:12.699
He was on a ship last time.

00:31:12.770 --> 00:31:14.670
You're mistaken.

00:31:14.739 --> 00:31:17.299
He was on the surface
when he was assimilated.

00:31:17.375 --> 00:31:18.933
No. He wasn't.

00:31:19.043 --> 00:31:21.273
A class-1 transport

00:31:21.346 --> 00:31:24.179
was detected in Grid 649...

00:31:24.249 --> 00:31:25.341
one life-form...

00:31:25.416 --> 00:31:27.976
species: Brunali.

00:31:39.564 --> 00:31:41.498
This better be important.

00:31:41.566 --> 00:31:43.158
It is.

00:31:43.234 --> 00:31:44.599
Sorry, I don't read Borg.

00:31:44.669 --> 00:31:45.966
You'll have
to translate.

00:31:46.037 --> 00:31:47.368
This is tactical data

00:31:47.438 --> 00:31:49.565
from the cube
where we found the children.

00:31:49.641 --> 00:31:50.972
It says that Icheb was alone

00:31:51.109 --> 00:31:52.838
aboard an unarmed
transport vessel

00:31:52.911 --> 00:31:54.105
when the Borg took him.

00:31:54.178 --> 00:31:56.203
Oh, why are you
telling me this

00:31:56.281 --> 00:31:58.146
at 0300 hours?

00:31:58.216 --> 00:32:00.650
Icheb's father told me
the boy was assimilated

00:32:00.718 --> 00:32:02.015
on the planet's surface.

00:32:02.086 --> 00:32:04.554
Is it possible
you misunderstood?

00:32:04.622 --> 00:32:07.056
No. He was very specific.

00:32:07.125 --> 00:32:09.059
That cube was disabled

00:32:09.127 --> 00:32:10.355
by a deadly pathogen.

00:32:10.428 --> 00:32:11.895
It suffered extensive damage.

00:32:11.963 --> 00:32:14.261
Isn't it possible
these records were corrupted?

00:32:14.332 --> 00:32:16.926
Perhaps, but I found
another inconsistency

00:32:17.001 --> 00:32:18.263
in Leucon's story.

00:32:18.336 --> 00:32:21.203
He told me Icheb was assimilated
four years ago,

00:32:21.272 --> 00:32:23.172
but further analysis indicates

00:32:23.241 --> 00:32:24.731
the Borg attacked three times

00:32:24.809 --> 00:32:26.071
during the last decade...

00:32:26.144 --> 00:32:27.668
nine years ago, six years ago

00:32:27.745 --> 00:32:29.042
and again last year.

00:32:31.049 --> 00:32:32.539
All right.

00:32:32.617 --> 00:32:35.484
Let's assume your information
is accurate.

00:32:35.553 --> 00:32:36.850
What does it prove?

00:32:36.921 --> 00:32:38.354
His father was lying.

00:32:38.423 --> 00:32:39.890
Why would he do that?

00:32:39.958 --> 00:32:41.949
I'm not certain, but we have

00:32:42.093 --> 00:32:43.754
an obligation to find out.

00:32:43.828 --> 00:32:45.352
What are you proposing?

00:32:45.430 --> 00:32:47.421
That we return to the planet,

00:32:47.498 --> 00:32:49.432
demand an explanation.

00:32:49.500 --> 00:32:51.297
Those people have
been through enough.

00:32:51.369 --> 00:32:53.200
Do we really need
to interrogate them?

00:32:53.271 --> 00:32:54.431
We have a responsibility

00:32:54.505 --> 00:32:55.733
to ensure Icheb's safety.

00:32:55.807 --> 00:32:59.607
He chose to stay
with his parents.

00:32:59.677 --> 00:33:01.406
Maybe he didn't have
all the information.

00:33:01.479 --> 00:33:04.277
Just because they weren't
completely candid with you

00:33:04.349 --> 00:33:05.281
doesn't mean
they're unfit parents.

00:33:05.350 --> 00:33:09.218
At some point...
you have to let go.

00:33:10.288 --> 00:33:12.552
I know what you're thinking...

00:33:12.623 --> 00:33:14.352
that I'm having
emotional difficulty

00:33:14.425 --> 00:33:16.586
accepting my separation
from Icheb.

00:33:16.661 --> 00:33:19.630
And you're correct,

00:33:19.697 --> 00:33:22.063
but if there's a possibility
he's in danger,

00:33:22.133 --> 00:33:23.100
even a remote one,

00:33:23.167 --> 00:33:26.159
I have to do whatever I can
to protect him.

00:33:26.237 --> 00:33:30.731
If I don't, I'll be no better
than my own parents.

00:33:33.878 --> 00:33:33.978
Couldn't we at least
wait a few days?

00:33:33.978 --> 00:33:35.741
Couldn't we at least
wait a few days?

00:33:35.813 --> 00:33:37.178
What would that accomplish?

00:33:37.248 --> 00:33:38.545
He's just
getting settled.

00:33:38.616 --> 00:33:39.878
The longer we wait,

00:33:39.951 --> 00:33:41.919
the harder it'll be
for everyone.

00:33:41.986 --> 00:33:43.886
You know that.

00:33:43.955 --> 00:33:45.582
Why do it at all?

00:33:45.656 --> 00:33:47.487
There's nothing compelling us

00:33:47.558 --> 00:33:50.322
to go through with it.

00:33:50.395 --> 00:33:52.625
It's what he was born for.

00:33:52.697 --> 00:33:54.961
Hasn't he been through enough?

00:33:55.033 --> 00:33:58.469
Why not give him a chance
at an ordinary life?

00:33:58.536 --> 00:34:00.527
He's not an ordinary child.

00:34:00.605 --> 00:34:02.334
No, but he can help us
in other ways.

00:34:02.407 --> 00:34:03.541
He's bright.

00:34:03.608 --> 00:34:04.666
He-he's hardworking...

00:34:04.742 --> 00:34:05.731
Leucon...

00:34:05.810 --> 00:34:07.778
his return was a gift.

00:34:07.845 --> 00:34:09.938
We can't waste it.

00:34:11.516 --> 00:34:14.041
I don't want to lose him
a second time.

00:34:14.118 --> 00:34:16.814
To survive, we all have
to make sacrifices.

00:34:16.888 --> 00:34:18.685
You taught me that.

00:34:20.525 --> 00:34:24.393
We won three games in a row.

00:34:25.763 --> 00:34:28.323
Sit down, Icheb.

00:34:33.738 --> 00:34:36.229
We need to talk.

00:34:42.580 --> 00:34:46.311
You know that
you're very important to us.

00:34:46.384 --> 00:34:48.318
Yes.

00:34:52.056 --> 00:34:54.354
What you don't know is why.

00:34:55.893 --> 00:34:57.520
What do you mean?

00:35:06.003 --> 00:35:07.197
What is that?

00:35:07.271 --> 00:35:09.330
If you relax, it won't hurt you.

00:35:09.407 --> 00:35:10.499
Father...

00:35:10.575 --> 00:35:12.634
You'd better hold him.

00:35:12.710 --> 00:35:15.406
What are you doing to me?

00:35:15.480 --> 00:35:17.414
No!

00:35:25.356 --> 00:35:27.881
Prepare the launch.

00:35:38.736 --> 00:35:40.260
Hail them.

00:35:42.406 --> 00:35:44.169
We didn't expect
to see you again, Captain.

00:35:44.242 --> 00:35:46.267
We'd like to ask you
a few questions,

00:35:46.344 --> 00:35:47.936
if you don't mind.

00:35:48.012 --> 00:35:49.479
Questions?

00:35:49.547 --> 00:35:50.809
Regarding Icheb

00:35:50.882 --> 00:35:52.782
and the circumstances
of his assimilation.

00:35:52.850 --> 00:35:54.841
We've already discussed that.

00:35:54.919 --> 00:35:58.184
The story you told me
was inconsistent with our data.

00:35:58.256 --> 00:36:00.554
We don't owe you
any explanations.

00:36:00.625 --> 00:36:02.889
In that case,
I'd like to talk to Icheb.

00:36:02.960 --> 00:36:04.552
He's not here.

00:36:04.629 --> 00:36:07.063
Where is he?

00:36:07.131 --> 00:36:09.156
That's not your concern.

00:36:09.233 --> 00:36:11.167
Scan for his bio-signs.

00:36:13.804 --> 00:36:15.897
He is not in the settlement.

00:36:15.973 --> 00:36:18.168
I'm detecting
a Brunali transport vessel.

00:36:18.242 --> 00:36:20.107
Distance:
Nine million kilometers.

00:36:20.178 --> 00:36:23.511
It's heading for the coordinates
of the transwarp conduit.

00:36:23.581 --> 00:36:25.742
According to these readings,

00:36:25.816 --> 00:36:27.750
that ship is traveling
at warp 9.8.

00:36:27.818 --> 00:36:29.012
It only looks that way.

00:36:29.086 --> 00:36:31.213
It's been designed to emit
a false warp signature...

00:36:31.289 --> 00:36:33.917
strong enough to
penetrate subspace.

00:36:34.025 --> 00:36:37.517
They're using it as bait
to attract the Borg.

00:36:37.595 --> 00:36:40.063
Icheb's on that vessel,
isn't he?

00:36:40.131 --> 00:36:42.429
He's fighting for his people.

00:36:42.500 --> 00:36:44.900
Alone, on an unarmed transport.

00:36:44.969 --> 00:36:46.630
We don't have particle weapons

00:36:46.704 --> 00:36:48.865
or powerful starships
at our disposal.

00:36:48.940 --> 00:36:52.068
We're forced to use
the only resource we have.

00:36:52.143 --> 00:36:53.405
Your children?

00:36:53.477 --> 00:36:54.535
No.

00:36:54.612 --> 00:36:56.705
Our genetic expertise.

00:36:56.781 --> 00:36:59.113
Icheb's not bait.

00:36:59.183 --> 00:37:00.548
He's a weapon.

00:37:00.618 --> 00:37:03.018
The first cube that captured him

00:37:03.087 --> 00:37:05.021
was infected by a pathogen.

00:37:05.089 --> 00:37:07.250
Icheb was the carrier,
wasn't he?

00:37:07.325 --> 00:37:09.555
Every time we try to rebuild,
begin to make progress,

00:37:09.627 --> 00:37:11.720
the Borg come
and take it away from us.

00:37:11.796 --> 00:37:14.128
Tom, set a course
for that transport vessel,

00:37:14.198 --> 00:37:15.130
full impulse.

00:37:15.199 --> 00:37:16.461
Aye, Captain.

00:37:16.534 --> 00:37:18.263
You have no right to interfere.

00:37:18.336 --> 00:37:20.201
We're trying to save
our civilization.

00:37:20.271 --> 00:37:22.205
By taking away Icheb's future.

00:37:22.273 --> 00:37:24.434
If we don't stop the Borg,

00:37:24.508 --> 00:37:26.908
the Brunali have no future.

00:37:26.978 --> 00:37:28.878
Captain, a Borg ship

00:37:28.946 --> 00:37:31.540
will emerge from that conduit
at any moment.

00:37:31.616 --> 00:37:32.810
You'll be destroyed.

00:37:32.883 --> 00:37:34.145
We'll take our chances.

00:37:34.218 --> 00:37:35.310
End transmission.

00:37:37.221 --> 00:37:41.385
Red Alert. Battle stations.

00:37:45.463 --> 00:37:46.930
We're coming within range,
Captain.

00:37:46.998 --> 00:37:47.930
I'm picking up

00:37:47.999 --> 00:37:49.193
Icheb's life-signs.

00:37:49.267 --> 00:37:51.360
Bio-scans indicate
he's unconscious.

00:37:51.435 --> 00:37:53.027
Transport him to Sick Bay.

00:37:53.104 --> 00:37:54.833
I can't. There's some kind
of interference.

00:37:54.905 --> 00:37:56.372
It's the conduit.

00:37:56.440 --> 00:37:58.533
By my estimate,
a Borg vessel will emerge

00:37:58.609 --> 00:37:59.906
in less than 40 seconds.

00:37:59.977 --> 00:38:02.036
Transfer auxiliary power
to the transporters.

00:38:03.948 --> 00:38:06.746
I still can't establish a lock,
not at this distance.

00:38:06.817 --> 00:38:07.875
30 seconds.

00:38:07.985 --> 00:38:10.146
Tom, get us closer to that ship.

00:38:10.221 --> 00:38:11.586
Yes, ma'am.

00:38:17.862 --> 00:38:19.523
The conduit's opening.
20 seconds.

00:38:19.597 --> 00:38:20.655
Seven?

00:38:20.731 --> 00:38:21.993
Still out of range.

00:38:22.066 --> 00:38:23.033
You heard her, Tom.

00:38:23.100 --> 00:38:24.692
When that Borg ship
comes through,

00:38:24.769 --> 00:38:27.431
I'm going to have a hell
of a time getting away from it.

00:38:27.505 --> 00:38:28.767
One problem at a time.

00:38:28.839 --> 00:38:29.897
Ten seconds...

00:38:30.007 --> 00:38:31.702
nine... eight...

00:38:31.776 --> 00:38:33.004
I've got a lock.

00:38:33.077 --> 00:38:34.339
Transport in progress.

00:38:34.412 --> 00:38:36.380
...five... four...
- He's in Sick Bay.

00:38:36.447 --> 00:38:38.347
Get us out of here, maximum...

00:38:43.954 --> 00:38:45.717
Target their tractor beam
generator.

00:38:45.790 --> 00:38:47.724
Phasers targeted.

00:38:47.792 --> 00:38:49.316
Fire.

00:38:53.030 --> 00:38:53.928
No effect.

00:38:54.065 --> 00:38:54.929
We are the Borg.

00:38:55.066 --> 00:38:57.159
You will be assimilated.

00:38:57.234 --> 00:38:58.929
Resistance is futile.

00:38:59.070 --> 00:39:00.128
Perhaps not.

00:39:00.204 --> 00:39:02.570
There is a way to get a weapon
through their shields.

00:39:02.640 --> 00:39:03.868
I'm listening.

00:39:03.941 --> 00:39:05.772
Transport a photon torpedo
to the Brunali vessel.

00:39:05.843 --> 00:39:07.674
Set it to detonate as soon
as it's inside the sphere.

00:39:07.745 --> 00:39:11.511
That will occur
in approximately 20 seconds.

00:39:11.582 --> 00:39:14.312
However, Voyager will be inside
less than three seconds later.

00:39:14.385 --> 00:39:15.647
Tom, full reverse thrusters.

00:39:15.720 --> 00:39:17.347
It might buy us
a couple more seconds.

00:39:17.421 --> 00:39:18.251
Do it.

00:39:21.459 --> 00:39:24.087
Transport complete.

00:39:24.161 --> 00:39:26.493
Detonation in
ten, nine...

00:39:30.568 --> 00:39:31.728
...five... four...

00:39:31.802 --> 00:39:33.064
Tom, go to warp on my mark.

00:39:33.137 --> 00:39:34.104
Three, two...

00:39:34.171 --> 00:39:35.604
All hands, brace for impact.

00:39:39.110 --> 00:39:41.510
Now, Mr. Paris!

00:39:44.582 --> 00:39:46.174
The Borg vessel has taken

00:39:46.250 --> 00:39:47.342
heavy damage.

00:39:47.418 --> 00:39:48.715
They are not pursuing.

00:39:57.027 --> 00:39:59.928
Are you saying
his parents reinfected him?

00:40:00.030 --> 00:40:01.930
No. They merely sedated him.

00:40:02.032 --> 00:40:03.624
I don't understand.

00:40:03.701 --> 00:40:05.794
He was genetically engineered

00:40:05.870 --> 00:40:09.271
to produce the pathogen...
from birth.

00:40:10.975 --> 00:40:12.670
Bred to kill Borg.

00:40:12.743 --> 00:40:14.404
Is he in danger?

00:40:14.478 --> 00:40:16.412
I can suppress the pathogen.

00:40:16.480 --> 00:40:19.574
He'll be fine... physically.

00:40:21.852 --> 00:40:23.183
He's going to need help

00:40:23.254 --> 00:40:25.415
coming to terms
with what's happened.

00:40:25.489 --> 00:40:26.820
Captain, I...

00:40:26.891 --> 00:40:28.859
Use your maternal instincts.

00:40:28.926 --> 00:40:30.450
They worked before.

00:40:46.310 --> 00:40:47.971
I thought you were studying

00:40:48.078 --> 00:40:49.602
spatial harmonics.

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:52.843
My parents suggested
I might have an aptitude

00:40:52.917 --> 00:40:55.112
for genetics as well.

00:40:57.188 --> 00:40:58.348
I see.

00:41:04.261 --> 00:41:06.525
What have you learned?

00:41:06.597 --> 00:41:10.590
This is the genome
of a typical Brunali male...

00:41:10.668 --> 00:41:13.603
and this is my DNA.

00:41:13.671 --> 00:41:15.536
They're nearly identical,

00:41:15.606 --> 00:41:18.166
but do you notice
the differences

00:41:18.242 --> 00:41:21.370
in the third, 13th
and 17th chromosomes?

00:41:21.445 --> 00:41:22.776
Yes.

00:41:22.847 --> 00:41:25.407
My parents made
microgenetic alterations

00:41:25.483 --> 00:41:27.610
so I would produce the pathogen.

00:41:27.685 --> 00:41:29.846
Quite ingenious.

00:41:31.222 --> 00:41:33.213
It's also barbaric.

00:41:33.290 --> 00:41:35.758
They were trying
to defend themselves...

00:41:35.826 --> 00:41:37.054
their way of life...

00:41:37.127 --> 00:41:39.561
preserve their species.

00:41:39.630 --> 00:41:41.860
I know how difficult it is

00:41:41.932 --> 00:41:44.958
to acknowledge
your parents' faults,

00:41:45.102 --> 00:41:47.570
but what they did was wrong.

00:41:47.638 --> 00:41:50.368
You don't have to forgive them.

00:41:50.441 --> 00:41:54.377
Do you think
they will ever forgive me?

00:41:54.445 --> 00:41:56.174
For what?

00:41:56.247 --> 00:41:58.875
I could have destroyed
that sphere.

00:41:58.949 --> 00:42:00.814
I failed them.

00:42:00.885 --> 00:42:02.648
You would have been
reassimilated.

00:42:02.720 --> 00:42:05.314
I know, but...

00:42:05.389 --> 00:42:07.721
But what?

00:42:07.791 --> 00:42:10.760
Maybe it was my destiny.

00:42:12.763 --> 00:42:14.230
Maybe.

00:42:16.767 --> 00:42:19.429
In the future, you may choose
to fight the Borg,

00:42:19.503 --> 00:42:21.403
but you'll do it
in your own way.

00:42:23.574 --> 00:42:25.166
You're an individual,

00:42:25.242 --> 00:42:29.178
and you have the right
to determine your own destiny.

00:42:31.815 --> 00:42:34.215
It's time to regenerate.

00:42:40.424 --> 00:42:42.619
And if I prefer
to continue studying?

00:42:47.298 --> 00:42:49.596
It's your decision.
